tasks.details:
1. Rewrite includes/class-ajax-handler.php for DR_Subs_AJAX_Handler
2. Register AJAX actions: wp_ajax_dr_subs_get_fix_preview, wp_ajax_dr_subs_apply_fix, wp_ajax_dr_subs_revert_fix, wp_ajax_dr_subs_run_scan, wp_ajax_dr_subs_cancel_scan, wp_ajax_dr_subs_save_settings
3. Each handler: verify nonce (DR_Subs_Security::verify_nonce), check manage_woocommerce capability, sanitize inputs
4. get_fix_preview: load sub, load rule, call preview_fix(), check if AS action already executed (for revert warning), render modal-fix-preview.php partial, return HTML
5. apply_fix: load sub, load rule, call apply_fix() with state guard, record journal entry, return JSON {success, entry_id, message}
6. revert_fix: load journal entry, check state drift, call rule's revert_fix(), return JSON {success, message, warnings[]}
7. run_scan: check transient lock, trigger DR_Subs_Health_Scanner::run() async (wp_schedule_single_event immediate), return JSON {success}
8. cancel_scan: set cancellation flag (transient dr_subs_scan_cancel), scanner checks between batches, return JSON {success}
9. save_settings: validate alerts_enabled (bool), alert_email (email), journal_retention_days (int 30-365 or -1), telemetry_enabled (bool), update_option('dr_subs_settings'), return JSON {success}

1. Dashboard.php: add 'Fix all N ghost subs' button when ghost_sub matches exist
2. AJAX handler wp_ajax_dr_subs_bulk_fix: receive rule_id + sub_ids array, generate batch_id (uniqid()), iterate subs calling rule's apply_fix(), all journal entries share batch_id, return JSON {success, batch_id, fixed_count, errors[]}
3. Revert batch: AJAX handler wp_ajax_dr_subs_revert_batch receives batch_id, load all entries with that batch_id, call revert_fix() on each atomically (transaction if possible, else sequential with rollback tracking), return JSON {success, reverted_count}
4. Journal cleanup: register Action Scheduler recurring action dr_subs_journal_cleanup (weekly), calls DR_Subs_Fix_Journal::purge_older_than(get_option('dr_subs_settings')['journal_retention_days'])
5. Handle retention_days=-1 special case: never purge
6. Bulk fix UI shows progress bar via JS polling (check scan status transient)
